ca","oracle_text":"Exile all nonland permanents target player controls. Return the exiled cards to the battlefield under their owner's control at the beginning of the next end step.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2012-02-03","toughness":null,"type_line":"Sorcery"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["R"],"colors":["R"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"commander":"legal","duel":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{R}","name":"Lightning Bolt","oracle_id":"4457ed35-7c10-48c8-9776-456485fdf070","oracle_text":"Lightning Bolt deals 3 damage to any target.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":["B","U"],"colors":["B","U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}{U}{B}","name":"Mnemonic Betrayal","oracle_id":"aa41e0e6-d04e-48d6-8450-02b972dd0bb1","oracle_text":"Exile all opponents' graveyards. You may cast spells from among those cards this turn, and mana of any type can be spent to cast them. At the beginning of the next end step, if any of those cards remain exiled, return them to their owners' graveyards.\nExile Mnemonic Betrayal.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2018-10-05","toughness":null,"type_line":"Sorcery"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If you Donate an Aura, it stays where it is, but the targeted player now controls it.","oracle_id":"049d1fb2-cce7-40e7-a633-e84cf9782d89","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Pull from Eternity affects a card that’s haunting a creature, the haunt effect ends.","oracle_id":"2903bd66-6948-445b-a18a-12e2ce1a86c3","published_at":"2006-09-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Pull from Eternity affects a suspended card, the card loses its time counters and is no longer suspended. (This doesn’t trigger the last ability of suspend.)","oracle_id":"2903bd66-6948-445b-a18a-12e2ce1a86c3","published_at":"2006-09-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Pull from Eternity targets a card in the exile zone. A card is only face down in the exile zone if the effect that put it there specifically says so.","oracle_id":"2903bd66-6948-445b-a18a-12e2ce1a86c3","published_at":"2006-09-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Although Darksteel Citadel is an artifact, it can't be cast as a spell. Playing it follows the normal rules for playing a land.","oracle_id":"8dc067bf-f78f-4ac4-b6e7-b305c42cf0bc","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the creature this Aura would enchant is an illegal target by the time Rancor tries to resolve, the Aura spell doesn't resolve. It won't enter the battlefield, so it won't be put into a graveyard from the battlefield and its ability won't trigger.","oracle_id":"9d2d6479-531c-4ce1-b52b-00e36fa63b64","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An activated ability has a \"Cost: Effect\" format. Look for the colon. A triggered ability starts with \"when\", \"whenever\", or \"at\".","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"It can target delayed triggered abilities. For example, a card that says \"Whenever a player cycles a card, you may exile target creature. If you do, return that creature to the battlefield at the beginning of the end step.\" triggers when a player cycles a card and creates a delayed trigger that happens at the beginning of the end step. You can choose to target the \"at the beginning of the end step\" trigger when it is placed on the stack at end of turn.","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Turn-based actions and special actions like the normal card draw, combat damage, or turning a face-down creature face up can't be targeted.","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Auras attached to the exiled creatures will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled creatures will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled creatures will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"c8981af1-b0aa-4c19-8520-a7fb59018bc8","published_at":"2024-01-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature token is exiled, it ceases to exist. It won't be returned to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"c8981af1-b0aa-4c19-8520-a7fb59018bc8","published_at":"2024-01-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Sudden Disappearance’s delayed triggered ability is countered or otherwise removed from the stack after triggering, the exiled cards will remain in exile indefinitely. The delayed triggered ability will only trigger once.","oracle_id":"dbe28518-d795-4bc5-afa6-63c696c86fca","published_at":"2011-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Mnemonic Betrayal doesn’t change when you can cast the exiled cards. For example, if you exile a sorcery card, you can cast it only during your main phase when the stack is empty.","oracle_id":"aa41e0e6-d04e-48d6-8450-02b972dd0bb1","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can’t play land cards exiled this way.","oracle_id":"aa41e0e6-d04e-48d6-8450-02b972dd0bb1","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Only the cards that remain in exile are returned to their owners’ graveyards. For example, a permanent spell cast this way will remain on the battlefield.","oracle_id":"aa41e0e6-d04e-48d6-8450-02b972dd0bb1","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any spells or permanents you control from Mnemonic Betrayal’s effect are exiled. If you leave the game before Mnemonic Betrayal’s delayed triggered ability resolves, the cards remain exiled.","oracle_id":"aa41e0e6-d04e-48d6-8450-02b972dd0bb1","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you cast a spell this way and that card is exiled, it’s considered a new object. Mnemonic Betrayal no longer allows you to cast it. It remains in exile when Mnemonic Betrayal’s delayed triggered ability resolves.","oracle_id":"aa41e0e6-d04e-48d6-8450-02b972dd0bb1","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
